    "created_at": "2026-11-22T14:49:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T14:49:04Z",
    "body": "Facts from the second read of PR #3421 (comment 7080818064 on that PR), for the decision of this issue:\n\n- The first feed that turns A and B while the tool goes down is checked by the verifier rules for a move whose pose changes: the mid-turn sweep (`crates/sim/src/verify/sweep.rs`, `turn_cells.rs`, `tilt_span.rs`), the mid-move pose checks (`midpose.rs`) and the fixture sweep (`posed_steel.rs`). With PR #3421 the pose at the start of that move is a commanded pose, so the check starts from a known state.\n- The return of the rotary axes to zero is in a rapid at the clearance of the section, after the Z retract and before the approach. The read recommends one more step for this issue: turn the rotary axes alone at the tool-change height, before the X/Y traverse. Reason: with tool centre point control active, a rapid that the control does not interpolate as a straight line can let the tip go below the clearance, and a tilt of more than 90 degrees from the program before can put the head body below the tip.\n- \"Upright\" is the literal angle zero on each rotary axis (`crates/post/src/post/mod.rs:539-541`). That is true for each machine file that ships. A machine with a home angle that is not zero needs a mapping through the kinematics.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
